{{Politics of the United States}}

'''Visa requirements for [[United States nationality law|United States citizens]]''' are administrative entry restrictions by the authorities of other states that are imposed on [[citizens of the United States]].
{{As of|2026}}, holders of a [[United States passport]] may travel to 179 countries and territories without a [[travel visa]], or with a [[visa on arrival]]. The United States passport ranks{{refn|group=Note|name=Ranking| Using [[Ranking#Dense ranking ("1223" ranking)|dense ranking]].}} 10th in terms of travel freedom, according to the [[Henley Passport Index]].<ref>{{cite web | title=Global Ranking - Visa Passport Index | url=https://www.henleyglobal.com/passport-index/ranking | publisher=Henley & Partner s| access-date=September 11, 2025}}</ref> It is also ranked 8th by the [[The Passport Index|Global Passport Power Rank]].<ref name=":12">{{Cite web|url=https://www.passportindex.org/byRank.php|title=Global Passport Power Rank 2026 &#124; Passport Index 2026|website=Passportindex.org|access-date=July 25, 2026}}</ref>

